<title>USA: Richmond Fed manufacturing, services indexes rose.</title>
<headline>Richmond Fed manufacturing, services indexes rose.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond said its indexes monitoring manufacturing and service-sector activity were higher in October compared with September.</p>
<p> MANUFACTURING SURVEY     Oct	    Sept</p>
<p>  Shipments		     4		 2</p>
<p>  New Orders		    2		-4</p>
<p>  Backlog Orders	     -9	     -12</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	 1		 2</p>
<p>  Average workweek	    4		 0</p>
<p>  Prices received	  0.15	    0.01</p>
<p>  Prices paid		0.35	    0.34</p>
<p> SERVICES SURVEY	    Oct	    Sept</p>
<p>  Service revenues	   17		-2</p>
<p>  Number of Employees	 2		-3</p>
<p>  Service wage		 22		14</p>
<p>  Retail revenues	     7		18</p>
<p>  Retail employees	  -14	     -10</p>
<p>  Retail wage		  28		14</p>
<p>  Shopper traffic	   -11		 4</p>
</text>
